# C++ programs inside Zoraya (TASK-30, proposed ADR-0360 to ADR-0366; `make
# test-cxx`): tests/cxx/'s programs built by zc++ against libc++, libc++abi and
# libunwind, on rootfs/ with /bin/cxxtest, /bin/hello, /work/granted and
# /work/secret. cxxtest runs through the broker with its description
# (user/describe/posix/cxxtest.cmd), hello through posixrun.
! panicked
! ZORAYA-PANIC
! cxxtest: FAIL
< \r\n~> 
# iostream, a static constructor, a caught exception.
> posixrun /bin/hello\r
< hello from C++: caught
< posixrun: exit 0
< \r\n~> 
# Thrown 20 frames down and caught with every destructor run; rethrow; a
# constructor that throws; bad_alloc, out_of_range, system_error from the
# library; exception_ptr out of a std::thread; a future's exception.
> cxxtest exceptions\r
< cxxtest: exceptions passed
< \r\n~> 
> status\r
< \r\nsucceeded (exit status 0)
< \r\n~> 
> cxxtest rtti\r
< cxxtest: rtti passed
< \r\n~> 
# Static constructors in definition order (checked inside), destructors in
# reverse order after main and atexit's handler.
> cxxtest statics\r
< cxxtest: statics passed
< cxxtest: atexit ran
< cxxtest: destroyed c
< cxxtest: destroyed b
< cxxtest: destroyed a
< \r\n~> 
# aligned_alloc, posix_memalign and aligned new (libposix's, ADR-0366).
> cxxtest alloc\r
< cxxtest: alloc passed
< \r\n~> 
> cxxtest threads\r
< cxxtest: threads passed
< \r\n~> 
# thread_local destructors at each thread's exit (__cxa_thread_atexit).
> cxxtest tls\r
< cxxtest: tls passed
< \r\n~> 
# notify_all_at_thread_exit and set_value_at_thread_exit only after the
# thread's thread_local destructors (__cxa_thread_atexit_impl, musl patch
# 0003): 200 rounds each, a destructor that gives the CPU away.
> cxxtest exit-order\r
< cxxtest: exit-order passed
< \r\n~> 
# cout and cerr, string streams, a file of the program's own /tmp, the C
# locale (musl takes a name and keeps the C rules under it: ADR-0363), regex,
# random_device.
> cxxtest iostream /tmp\r
< cxxtest: cout 42 2.5 ff
< cxxtest: cerr line
< cxxtest: locale de_DE.UTF-8 named de_DE.UTF-8, decimal point .
< cxxtest: iostream passed
< \r\n~> 
> cxxtest fsops /tmp\r
< cxxtest: fsops passed
< \r\n~> 
# std::filesystem lists the directory the line grants and is refused the one
# it does not (a path outside the table is ENOENT, ADR-0107); the shell says
# which grant was missing.
> +r /work/granted cxxtest fs /work/granted /work/secret\r
< cxxtest: /work/granted: one.txt sub/ two.txt
< cxxtest: /work/secret: No such file or directory
< hint: cxxtest tried to read /work/secret, which it was not given
< \r\n~> 
> status\r
< \r\nexit status 1
< \r\n~> 
> cxxtest fs /work/granted\r
< cxxtest: /work/granted: No such file or directory
< \r\n~> 
# An exception nobody catches, one out of a noexcept function, and
# std::terminate: libc++abi's message, abort(), SIGABRT (ADR-0362).
> cxxtest uncaught\r
< libc++abi: terminating due to uncaught exception of type std::runtime_error: nobody catches this
< cxxtest: ended by signal 6
< \r\n~> 
> status\r
< \r\nended by signal 6
< \r\n~> 
> cxxtest noexcept\r
< libc++abi: terminating due to uncaught exception of type std::logic_error: out of a noexcept function
< cxxtest: ended by signal 6
< \r\n~> 
> cxxtest terminate\r
< libc++abi: terminating
< cxxtest: ended by signal 6
< \r\n~> 
# The fast hardening mode (ADR-0360): an index past the end traps.
> cxxtest hardening\r
< cxxtest: about to read v[2]
< cxxtest: crashed (breakpoint, class 0x3c)
< \r\n~> 
> status\r
< \r\ncrashed (breakpoint, class 0x3c)
< \r\n~> 
> poweroff\r
